/-! # Descent of ordinary blowup chart comparisons

Source: ILO, Exposé VIII, proof of 3.4.6, printed p. 111; Stacks Project,
Tags 0804, 0805, 0806, 022C, 022D and 023Q
(blueprint: lem-trf-etale-blowup-chart-descent).

The ideals `K i` are the affine ideals of `J.comap (g i)`, transported from
sections of `Spec (A i)` along the canonical `Scheme.ΓSpecIso`. The isomorphisms
`θ i` are over `Spec (A i)`; no overlap compatibility is assumed.
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u v

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData

/-- Independently given affine étale blowup comparisons descend uniquely over the base.
Source: ILO, Exposé VIII, proof of 3.4.6, printed p. 111, expanded by Stacks
Tags 0804, 0805, 0806, 022C, 022D and 023Q
(blueprint: lem-trf-etale-blowup-chart-descent).

Proof plan (the seven steps of the DAG):
1. On each chart, the affine extended ideal is `K i` extended to `A_i[K_i/a]`
   (lemma-nagata-extended-ideal-affine-chart). It is generated by `a`
   (lemma-nagata-chart-extended-ideal-principal), and multiplication by `a` is
   injective (lemma-nagata-chart-generator-regular). The finite generator charts
   cover (prop-nagata-affine-blowup-chart-cover), so pullback by `θ i` makes the
   ideal locally free of rank one on `Z_i`.
2. For flat `T → Z_i`, localizing preserves injectivity of multiplication by `a`.
   Tensoring this injection with the flat stalk algebra preserves injectivity
   (def-weil-flat-morphism, def-weil-pbc-flat-ring-map). The image of the pulled-back
   ideal is the extended ideal (lemma-nagata-flat-pullback-ideal-pow at exponent one,
   def-pc-module-pullback). Successive ideal extension is extension along the
   composite by the fibre-product definition of def-nagata-extended-ideal. Thus
   `J O_T` is invertible on the inverse images of these covering charts.
3. The jointly surjective étale family is an fpqc cover
   (def-weil-pbc-etale-site, lem-weil-pbc-fpqc-finer-than-etale).
   Its base changes to `Z`, `B` and all overlaps are fpqc covers
   (lem-galois-fpqc-covering-base-change, def-weil-pbc-fpqc-covering).
   In particular overlap projections are flat, so step 2 applies.
4. Compose `θ i` with the canonical flat comparison
   (thm-nagata-blowup-flat-base-change, def-nagata-blowup-flat-base-change-map).
   The two maps from an overlap to `B` agree by uniqueness of the lift from a
   scheme with invertible extended ideal (thm-nagata-blowup-universal-property).
   The invertible quotient is forced by its inclusion into the structure sheaf.
5. Descend these compatible maps by lem-weil-pbc-fpqc-representable-descent.
   Their composites to `X` agree locally with `q`, hence globally. The
   fibre-product universal property identifies each base change with the
   specified composite (def-pc-fibre-product).
6. The inverses of the local comparisons agree on overlaps: equality of the
   forward maps and of their two base projections implies equality of the
   pullback isomorphisms, hence of their inverses (def-pc-fibre-product).
   Descend the inverses over the fpqc cover of `B` by the same descent theorem.
7. Both global composites restrict to identities, so descent uniqueness gives
   both inverse identities and uniqueness of the descended isomorphism
   (lem-weil-pbc-fpqc-representable-descent). Its base changes are those of step 5.
-/
theorem etale_blowup_chart_descent
    {X Z : Scheme.{u}} (q : Z ⟶ X) (J : X.IdealSheafData)
    (hJ : Scheme.Modules.IsQuasiCoherentFiniteType J.toModules)
    {ι : Type v} (A : ι → CommRingCat.{u}) (g : ∀ i, Spec (A i) ⟶ X)
    [∀ i, Etale (g i)]
    (hg : ∀ x : X, ∃ i, ∃ y : Spec (A i), g i y = x)
    (K : ∀ i, Ideal (A i))
    (hK : ∀ i, K i = ((J.comap (g i)).ideal
      ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top (Spec (A i))⟩).map (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (A i)).hom.hom)
    (E : ∀ i, Finset (A i)) (hE : ∀ i, (E i).Nonempty)
    (hgen : ∀ i, Ideal.span (E i : Set (A i)) = K i)
    (hreg : ∀ i, ∀ a ∈ E i, Function.Injective (fun x : A i ↦ a * x))
    (θ : ∀ i, Over.mk (pullback.snd q (g i)) ≅ Over.mk (J.comap (g i)).blowupMap) :
    (∀ i, ∀ a ∈ E i,
      (K i).map (algebraMap (A i) (AffineBlowup.chartRing (K i) a)) =
        Ideal.span {algebraMap (A i) (AffineBlowup.chartRing (K i) a) a} ∧
      Function.Injective (fun x : AffineBlowup.chartRing (K i) a ↦
        algebraMap (A i) (AffineBlowup.chartRing (K i) a) a * x)) ∧
    (∀ i, ∀ (T : Scheme.{u}) (h : T ⟶ pullback q (g i)), Flat h →
      (J.comap (h ≫ pullback.fst q (g i) ≫ q)).IsInvertible) ∧
    (∀ i j,
      pullback.fst (pullback.fst q (g i)) (pullback.fst q (g j)) ≫
          (θ i).hom.left ≫ J.blowupFlatBaseChange (g i) ≫ pullback.fst J.blowupMap (g i) =
        pullback.snd (pullback.fst q (g i)) (pullback.fst q (g j)) ≫
          (θ j).hom.left ≫ J.blowupFlatBaseChange (g j) ≫
            pullback.fst J.blowupMap (g j)) ∧
    (∃! φ : Over.mk q ≅ Over.mk J.blowupMap,
      (∀ i, pullback.fst q (g i) ≫ φ.hom.left =
        (θ i).hom.left ≫ J.blowupFlatBaseChange (g i) ≫ pullback.fst J.blowupMap (g i)) ∧
      (∀ i, ((Over.pullback (g i)).mapIso φ).hom.left =
        (θ i).hom.left ≫ J.blowupFlatBaseChange (g i))) := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData
